            <ArticleTitle>Thumb Carpometacarpal Joint Stabilization in Ehlers-Danlos Syndrome--Case Report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>463-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1142/S021881041572020X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of an 18-years-old patient with thumb carpometacarpal ligament laxity due to Ehlers-Danlos syndrome who was treated with trapezial opening wedge osteotomy combined with volar ligaments reconstruction. Two years postoperatively she is pain free and the thumb carpometacarpal joint is stable.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
